APS-006 — Policy Decision Model

Document ID: APS-006
Title: Policy Decision Model
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Policy Decision Model (CPDM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Policy Decision Model establishes the standardized representation, semantics, governance, lifecycle, and traceability of decisions produced through policy evaluation.

Every policy evaluation SHALL produce one or more Canonical Policy Decisions.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Policy decision architecture
Decision structure
Decision semantics
Decision outcomes
Obligations
Recommendations
Justification
Decision governance

This specification applies to every policy decision produced within Atlas.

3. Canonical Definition

A Canonical Policy Decision (CPD) is a specialization of the Canonical Atlas Object representing the governed outcome of evaluating one or more Canonical Policy Objects against a defined evaluation context.

A Policy Decision records what the policies concluded.

It does not describe how the evaluation occurred.

4. Objectives

The Canonical Policy Decision SHALL:

Preserve evaluation outcomes.
Support explainability.
Preserve governance.
Preserve provenance.
Enable auditing.
Enable automation.
Support interoperability.
Support lifecycle management.
5. Inheritance

The Canonical Policy Decision SHALL inherit every mandatory property of the Canonical Atlas Object.

Canonical Atlas Object
        │
        ▼
Canonical Policy Decision
        │
 ┌──────┼──────────────┐
 ▼      ▼              ▼
Authorization Validation Workflow
 Decision      Decision   Decision

Future decision families SHALL extend this hierarchy.

6. Canonical Decision Structure

Every Canonical Policy Decision SHALL define:

Property	Description
Decision ID	Globally unique identifier
Decision Type	Canonical classification
Evaluation ID	Source evaluation
Policy References	Evaluated policies
Decision Status	Current lifecycle state
Decision Authority	Producing authority
Decision Timestamp	Time of creation
Decision Version	Version identifier
7. Decision Outcomes

Atlas defines the following canonical decision outcomes.

Outcome	Description
Permit	Action authorized
Deny	Action prohibited
Require	Action mandatory
Recommend	Advisory guidance
Warn	Warning issued
Escalate	Higher authority required
Defer	Decision postponed pending additional information

Every decision SHALL declare exactly one primary outcome.

8. Decision Context

Every decision SHALL preserve the complete evaluation context including:

Evaluated object(s)
Evaluation request
Applicable policies
Trust context
Workflow state
Lifecycle state
Organization
Project
Jurisdiction
Evaluation timestamp

The context SHALL be immutable after decision creation.

9. Decision Justification

Every decision SHALL include justification sufficient for independent review.

Justification SHALL identify:

Applicable policies
Conditions satisfied
Conditions failed
Conflict resolution steps
Supporting evidence
Final rationale

Justification SHALL remain permanently associated with the decision.

10. Decision Confidence

Where applicable, a decision MAY include a confidence assessment.

Atlas defines the following confidence levels.

Level	Meaning
C0	Unknown
C1	Low confidence
C2	Moderate confidence
C3	High confidence
C4	Very high confidence
C5	Certain within defined policy assumptions

Confidence SHALL NOT replace deterministic outcomes.

It provides additional evaluation metadata.

11. Generated Obligations

A Canonical Policy Decision MAY generate obligations.

Each obligation SHALL define:

Obligation identifier
Responsible participant
Required action
Completion criteria
Due date
Escalation conditions
Current status

Obligations SHALL be independently traceable.

12. Recommendations

Policy decisions MAY generate recommendations.

Recommendations SHALL define:

Suggested action
Supporting rationale
Priority
Optionality
Related engineering objectives

Recommendations SHALL NOT override mandatory decisions.

13. Decision Relationships

Policy Decisions MAY relate to:

Canonical Policy Objects
Decision Records
Canonical Events
Canonical Atlas Objects
Workflow Executions
Validation Results
Compliance Assessments

Relationships SHALL conform to ADS-011 — Relationship Model.

14. Decision Lifecycle

Every Canonical Policy Decision SHALL support:

Created
    │
Validated
    │
Approved
    │
Issued
    │
Implemented
    │
Closed
    │
Archived

Lifecycle transitions SHALL be governed.

15. Decision Governance

Every decision SHALL define:

Decision owner
Evaluation authority
Review authority
Approval authority
Applicable governance policies
Audit requirements

Governance SHALL remain attached throughout the decision lifecycle.

16. Decision Quality

Every Canonical Policy Decision SHALL satisfy:

Correctness
Explainability
Traceability
Determinism
Completeness
Consistency
Governance compliance
Auditability

Quality SHALL be measurable.

17. Conformance

A Canonical Policy Decision conforms if it:

Inherits the CAO contract.
References a valid policy evaluation.
Declares a canonical decision outcome.
Preserves evaluation context.
Includes justification.
Supports lifecycle management.
Maintains governance metadata.
18. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Probabilistic decision support.
Multi-authority policy decisions.
Distributed decision consensus.
AI-assisted decision recommendations.
Federated decision registries.
Real-time adaptive decision updates.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical decision semantics.

